      "status": "FINISHED",
      "focus": true,
      "results": {
        "code": "SUCCESS",
        "msg": [
          {
            "type": "HTML",
            "data": "<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>Discount k-mer counter</h2>\n<p>This notebook demonstrates elastic k-mer analysis with Apache Spark.<br />\nBy default, this notebook loads a small 10k reads file shipped with Discount. Please refer to the Discount README for further details.</p>\n<p>The paragraphs below contain examples of various kinds of data analysis and visualization. You can easily clone and edit paragraphs if you wish to make changes to parameters. The Discount API documentation, available at <a href=\"https://jtnystrom.github.io/Discount/com/jnpersson/discount/spark/index.html\">https://jtnystrom.github.io/Discount/com/jnpersson/discount/spark/index.html</a>, may be used as a reference.</p>\n<p>The code examples in this notebook are written in the Scala language. Before doing anything else, please configure and run the paragraphs &ldquo;spark settings&rdquo; and &ldquo;initial setup&rdquo;. After this, any of the other paragraphs can be run.<br />\nA paragraph can be run by pressing shift + enter when it is selected. Zeppelin&rsquo;s documentation and included tutorial notebooks, which should be accessible on the menus, may also be helpful to learn the basics of Zeppelin.</p>\n<p>If the notebook becomes stuck or unresponsive for some reason, it may help to use the gear wheel menu to restart the Spark interpreter.</p>\n<p>Additional information, as well as the latest version of Discount, is available from the GitHub repo at <a href=\"https://github.com/jtnystrom/Discount\">https://github.com/jtnystrom/Discount</a>.</p>\n\n</div>"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Spark settings",
      "text": "%spark.conf\n\n#Path to Discount jar - configure this\nspark.jars /path/to/Discount/target/scala-2.12/Discount-assembly-4.0.0.jar\n\n#If running a local Spark installation (not in a cloud), increase this setting as much as possible\nspark.driver.memory 16g\n\n#For local Spark, set the path to a Spark 3.5+ installation (if not configured elsewhere)\nSPARK_HOME /fast/spark-3.5.1-bin-hadoop3\n\n#For local spark, it is helpful to set a path to a SSD drive or other fast filesystem (for temporary files)\n#Note that this directory can get large. It will be cleared when you stop or restart the Spark interpreter in Zeppelin.\nspark.local.dir /fast/spark\n\n\n",
      "user": "anonymous",
      "dateUpdated": "2026-07-08T23:22:01+0900",
